---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Fix DroidDeck Game Crashes — DroidDeck Guide"
  description="Step-by-step fix for DroidDeck game crashes and force closes. Common causes and verified solutions."
  page="troubleshooting"

  locale="en"
>
  <style>
    .page-header{background:var(--night);color:white;padding:90px 0 50px}
    .page-header h1{font-size:36px;margin-bottom:12px}
    .page-header p{color:#93a7ba;max-width:600px}
    .page-content{padding:50px 0 80px;max-width:820px}
    .fix-section{margin-bottom:42px}
    .fix-section h2{font-size:24px;margin-bottom:14px}
    .fix-section p{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.9}
    .fix-section ol{padding-left:22px;font-size:15px;color:#43576c;line-height:1.9}
    .fix-section li{margin:10px 0}
    .callout{padding:16px 20px;background:#f0fdf4;border-left:4px solid #16a34a;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin:20px 0}
    .callout p{margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#166534;line-height:1.7}
    .tag-list{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px}
    .tag{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:5px 12px;border-radius:999px;background:#f0f7fc;color:#147cb9}
  </style>
  
    <section class="page-header">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="hero-label"><span></span> Troubleshooting</div>
        <h1>Game crashes / force close</h1>
        <p>Game exits during startup, loading, or gameplay.</p>
        <div class="tag-list">
          <span class="tag">RAM</span>
          <span class="tag">Thermal</span>
          <span class="tag">Compatibility</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-content wrap">
      <div class="fix-section">
        <h2>Common causes</h2>
        <p>Crashes usually come from insufficient RAM, thermal throttling, incompatible game settings, or a Proton/Wine prefix that needs resetting.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fix-section">
        <h2>Step-by-step fixes</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Close background apps.</strong> Free up RAM before launching DroidDeck. Large games need 6 GB or more available.</li>
          <li><strong>Lower graphics settings.</strong> Reduce resolution, texture quality, and shadow quality. Try 720p Low as a baseline.</li>
          <li><strong>Use active cooling.</strong> Phones especially throttle under sustained load. A clip-on fan can prevent thermal crashes.</li>
          <li><strong>Try a different Proton version.</strong> Some games crash on default Proton but run fine on Proton GE or an older build.</li>
          <li><strong>Reset the Proton prefix.</strong> Delete the game's prefix folder and let Steam recreate it. This fixes corrupt configuration files.</li>
          <li><strong>Verify game files.</strong> In Steam, right-click the game → Properties → Installed Files → Verify integrity.</li>
          <li><strong>Check available storage.</strong> Ensure you have at least 2–3 GB free beyond the game's install size for cache and swap.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="callout">
          <p>If the crash happens at the same point every time, it's likely game-specific. If it happens randomly, suspect RAM or thermals.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fix-section">
        <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
        <p>Report the crash with device model, DroidDeck version, game title, Proton version, and where the crash happens. Screenshots of any error dialog help a lot.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  
  
</Layout>
